  "profiling_findings": [
    "The /analytics/executive-summary endpoint was slow (~1.5s) because it sequentially called three expensive analytics functions.",
    "The get_market_intelligence_data function was identified as a major bottleneck due to fetching entire ORM model objects for the CompetitorPriceHistory table (100k+ rows) instead of specific columns.",
    "The get_strategy_distribution_all_products function was also fetching full ORM objects for competitor prices."
  ],
  "optimizations_performed": [
    "Modified db.query(CompetitorPriceHistory) to db.query(CompetitorPriceHistory.product_id, CompetitorPriceHistory.price, ...) in competitor_service.py to fetch Row tuples instead of full ORM objects.",
    "Applied the same ORM column selection optimization to analytics_service.py to reduce SQL instantiation overhead.",
    "Verified that ML models are properly pre-loaded via the singleton pattern (demand_predictor), confirming ML inference is not a bottleneck."
  ],
